      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RULESOFADMIRATION (8) won the latest of 2 trials this season, and meets a fairly modest field for her debut. A good draw helps, and with the blinkers on, she is expected to be positive early on. Hard to beat, especially if the money comes for her. MAGNIFICENT MALCOM (1) will find this far easier than his last start at Ascot in 3YO open company, and dropping back from 1400m to 1200m will also help his cause. Stick with him on an each-way basis. EZE BIG CARL (5) has been improving at each of his 4 public trials, and is now ready to make his debut. He is bred to want more ground, so expect him to be running on strongly. CATCHYA STAR (4) makes his debut after producing his best trial yet, finishing second at Lark less than 2 weeks ago. Include in all combos. BLIND SHOT (3) might improve on race day, so keep an eye on the markets for a guide.",
